Here is the simplest setup. We will use one file named config.properties to control everything.
1. The Config File (config.properties)
Create this file in your project folder (where pom.xml is). This is where you set your path.
Copy this content into config.properties:
# CHANGE THIS PATH below to point to your text file
source.file.path=C:/Users/YourName/Documents/my_input.txt

2. The Java Code (AsciiApp.java)
This single file reads your config, finds the text file, and processes it.
package com.example.ascii;

import org.springframework.boot.CommandLineRunner;
import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.util.Properties;
import java.util.List;

@SpringBootApplication
public class AsciiApp implements CommandLineRunner {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(AsciiApp.class, args);
    }

    @Override
    public void run(String... args) {
        try {
            // 1. LOAD CONFIG FILE
            Properties config = new Properties();
            // We look for 'config.properties' in the project root
            config.load(new FileInputStream("config.properties")); 

            // 2. GET THE PATH
            String filePath = config.getProperty("source.file.path");
            System.out.println("Reading file from: " + filePath);

            // 3. READ & PROCESS THE FILE
            List<String> lines = Files.readAllLines(Paths.get(filePath));
            
            // (Your ASCII Logic here - printing simple box for now)
            System.out.println("--------------------------------");
            lines.forEach(line -> System.out.println("| " + line));
            System.out.println("--------------------------------");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("ERROR: " + e.getMessage());
            System.err.println("Make sure 'config.properties' exists and the path inside it is correct.");
        }
    }
}

3. Summary: Where do you change the path?
You never touch the Java code to change the file.
 * Open config.properties.
 * Edit the line source.file.path=....
 * Save and run.
